{
  "about": "The fields an item's, armour set's, creature's or creature maturity's stats can hold: each field's label, its unit, the type of its value, and where it is used (the Items page's categories, \"sets\" for the armour sets of sets.json, whose stats every piece of the set has alike, \"creatures\", \"maturities\", \"skills\"). A value is stored in this unit whatever unit its source printed. Protection, durability and damage are one field per damage type (protection_stab, durability_cut, damage_burn and so on), as the game's item window listed them (\"Protection Stab\", \"Durability Cut\", \"Damage Burn\"); durability is the one figure a source gave where it gave no types, as the window did from 2006, a type the window left out having no value; damage_total is the total a player site gave where it gave no types, which the window never showed; and a creature's damage_share_ fields are the share of its damage of each type. The fields of one group (a weapon's damage by type) are read together: the page shows, for a VU, the types of the one reading nearest it, so a type a later reading left out is not shown beside it. shown names, for an item category, the creatures or their maturities, the fields every one of them lists, in that order before any other, \"unknown\" where nothing gives a value, as the game's windows listed them; and a group one type of which is known lists all its types. A skills value is a list of {\"name\", \"hidden\"}; a recipe a list of {\"item\": <item id>, \"amount\"}; an items value a list of item ids (what a blueprint makes); a range [lowest, highest].",
